  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 330 AM EDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nHeat will continue to be the main story through most of the forecast \nthough a break from it may be in sight. Humid conditions are \nexpected to bring heat index values up towards advisory criteria by \nthe end of the work week. \n\nOvernight lows will also be on the rise with the return of the mid \n70s to much of the area. This doesn't do much in providing relief \nfrom the daytime heat; especially for vulnerable populations. Look \nafter each other, and keep an eye on pets and kids. Stay hydrated if \nyou plan to spend time outside.\n\nThunderstorm chances during the afternoon will be down to less than \n2 0% for much of the area through the week. The ridge is finally \nexpected to break down Saturday into Sunday. Isolated thunderstorms \nwill be possible on Saturday afternoon, becoming scattered come \nSunday but total rainfall is expected to be less than a quarter of \nan inch for much of the CWA.",
